-- title:
--   Commute GHalf Sandwich Split One Iff
-- statement:
--   **The one-tail head-tail relation is equivalent to pair-product commutation.**
--
--   Let $(m,q,d)$ have a field model, let $\psi_{AB}$ be a bipartite quantum state, let $F$ be a slice-indexed polynomial family, and let $\delta$ be an error threshold. Let $O_1$ and $R_1$ be the ordered and rotated head-tail families for one tail point, and let $P_L$ and $P_R$ be the two pair-product families obtained by placing the two completed slice effects in the two possible orders.
--
--   Write $\mathcal Q$ for the finite set of slice questions. Then
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDOpRel}_{\psi_{AB},\,\operatorname{Unif}(\mathcal Q\times\mathbb{F}_q)}
--   \!\left(O_1,R_1;\delta\right)
--   \quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
--   \operatorname{SDDOpRel}_{\psi_{AB},\,\operatorname{Unif}(\mathcal Q\times\mathcal Q)}
--   \!\left(P_L,P_R;\delta\right).
--   $$
--
--   The equivalence is the length-one specialization of the split reindexing and identifies the base half-sandwich commutation problem with the pair-product problem.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.commuteGHalfSandwich_split_one_iff`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/Pasting/ComparisonLemmas/CommuteGHalfSandwich/Setup/StepLemmas/Split.lean#L158-L217

